{number: 154}
{title: Just A Closer Walk with Thee}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] I am weak, but Thou art strong;
Jesus, [F7] keep me from all wrong;
I’ll be [Bb] satisfied as long
As I [Eb] walk, let me [Bb] walk [F7] close to [Bb] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb] Just a closer walk with Thee,
Grant it, [F7] Jesus, is my plea,
Daily [Bb] walking close to [Eb] Thee:
Let it [Bb] be, dear [F7] Lord, let it [Bb] be.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Through [Bb] this world of toil and snares,
If I [F7] falter, Lord, who cares?
Who with [Bb] me my burden shares?
None but [Eb] Thee, dear [Bb] Lord, [F7] none but [Bb] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
When [Bb] my feeble life is o’er,
Time for [F7] me will be no more;
Guide me [Bb] gently, safely o’er
To Thy [Eb] kingdom [Bb] shore, [F7] to Thy [Bb] shore.
{end_of_verse}
